# Platform Adapter Pattern

All platform integrations (publish, shoppable, content sources, video gen) MUST follow this structure:

```
lib/<feature>/index.js        ← core logic, platform-agnostic contract
lib/<feature>/adapters/
  youtube.js                  ← YouTube-specific implementation
  tiktok.js                   ← TikTok-specific implementation
  instagram.js                ← Instagram-specific implementation
```

## Rules

**✅ Core layer (`index.js`) MUST:**
- Define the input/output contract (what params in, what shape out)
- Select and invoke the correct adapter based on customer config
- Own retry logic, error normalisation, and logging
- Know nothing about platform-specific auth, payloads, or APIs

**✅ Adapter layer MUST:**
- Implement only one platform
- Own all platform-specific API calls, auth headers, and payload shapes
- Export a single named function matching the core contract

**❌ NEVER:**
- Put `if (platform === 'youtube')` blocks inside core logic
- Put retry/error normalisation inside an adapter
- Add a new platform by editing existing files — add a new adapter file only

## Adding a new platform

1. Create `lib/<feature>/adapters/<platform>.js`
2. Implement the contract interface
3. Register it in `lib/<feature>/index.js` adapter map
4. No other files change

## PR review check

Flag any PR that adds platform names, platform API URLs, or platform auth logic outside an `adapters/` directory.
